I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services like VirusTotal from this environment. If you run the following request yourself (using your own API key), you’ll get the related object descriptors you’re looking for:

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related?limit=10&cursor=abc
Headers:
  x-apikey: my_api
```

The response will look something like this (only the fields you requested are shown):

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "subdomain1.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "context_attributes": {
          "relationship_type": "subdomain_of",
          "confidence": 100
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "subdomain2.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "context_attributes": {
          "relationship_type": "subdomain_of",
          "confidence": 95
        }
      }
    }
    // ... up to 10 items
  ],
  "meta": {
    "continuation_cursor": "next_cursor_value"
  }
}
```

You would extract just the `id` and any `context_attributes` from each item in the `data` array. If you need help parsing that JSON in your code, let me know!
